---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Understand MutualLens use, uploaded-data limitations, availability and responsibility for locally saved reports."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">TERMS OF USE</p><h1>Understand your results.</h1><p
    class="lede"
  >
    MutualLens compares supplied follower and following data. Read these terms
    alongside the privacy policy. Updated September 18, 2026.
  </p>
  <h2>Use accounts you own or manage</h2><p>
    Use MutualLens with information you are authorized to process. The intended
    purpose is understanding your own or managed accounts, not covert
    monitoring, bypassing private-account controls, or collecting data for
    resale.
  </p>
  <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2><p>
    Automatic checking is currently unavailable. Uploaded reports describe the
    files you provide and may differ from current Instagram relationships.
    Missing or unreadable records can affect results and are explained in the
    report. A result is not proof that someone unfollowed you.
  </p><p>
    MutualLens does not promise unlimited capacity, uninterrupted availability,
    complete platform coverage, or a particular result. It does not automate
    unfollowing or determine why a relationship changed.
  </p>
  <h2>Your local copies</h2><p>
    You control whether to save snapshots and download reports. You are
    responsible for choosing an appropriate device and handling downloaded
    files. Clearing app-controlled snapshots does not remove copies elsewhere.
  </p>
  <h2>No affiliation</h2><p>
    MutualLens is an independent project by Arhaan Aggarwal, not an Instagram or
    Meta product. Instagram and Meta names are used descriptively.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href={sitePath('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> and <a
      href={sitePath('/contact/')}>project contact information</a
    >.
  </p>
</Page>
